{
  "name": "Retry with exponential backoff",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Retry with exponential backoff\n\n**Origin:** New demonstration example.\n\n**Run it:** Execute the workflow. The mock API fails twice with 503, then succeeds. Change `simulate` to `permanent` to see the dead-letter path.\n\nConnect the Postgres nodes to a credential for the `resilience` database after import.",
        "height": 300,
        "width": 460,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "cef8d8cb-bba7-56ea-a827-22d5a2723f6b",
      "name": "About this example",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -560,
        -380
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {},
      "id": "e5933052-1364-5aab-9131-8362cb299b05",
      "name": "Run example",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.manualTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        0,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// Replace this with your real request. \"simulate\" tells the mock API how to behave:\n// fail_times:N, rate_limit_times:N, permanent, slow:S, or ok.\nreturn [{\n  json: {\n    idempotency_key: `retry-demo-${$execution.id}`,\n    body: { simulate: 'fail_times:2', note: 'retry demo' },\n    max_attempts: 4,\n    base_delay_seconds: 1,\n    max_delay_seconds: 8,\n  },\n}];\n"
      },
      "id": "c89c0713-1d1c-55de-b8a3-1c1e357f1ff8",
      "name": "Build request",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        220,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "method": "POST",
        "url": "http://mock-api:8080/deliver",
        "sendHeaders": true,
        "headerParameters": {
          "parameters": [
            {
              "name": "Idempotency-Key",
              "value": "={{ $('Build request').first().json.idempotency_key }}"
            }
          ]
        },
        "sendBody": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "jsonBody": "={{ JSON.stringify($('Build request').first().json.body) }}",
        "options": {
          "timeout": 10000,
          "response": {
            "response": {
              "fullResponse": true,
              "neverError": true
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "id": "d2d2c3c1-b446-58ad-8fa3-4fce680e8dd0",
      "name": "Call API",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [
        440,
        0
      ],
      "onError": "continueErrorOutput"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const status = Number($json.statusCode ?? 0);\nconst networkError = $json.error ? String($json.error.message ?? $json.error) : null;\n\n// 408, 425, 429 and 5xx are usually worth retrying. Other 4xx responses mean\n// the request itself is wrong, and sending it again will fail the same way.\nlet outcome = 'permanent';\nif (!networkError && status >= 200 && status < 300) outcome = 'success';\nelse if (networkError || [408, 425, 429].includes(status) || status >= 500) outcome = 'transient';\n\nconst retryAfter = Number($json.headers?.['retry-after']);\n\nconst req = $('Build request').first().json;\nconst attempt = $runIndex + 1;\n\n// Exponential backoff with equal jitter, never shorter than Retry-After.\nconst exp = Math.min(req.max_delay_seconds, req.base_delay_seconds * 2 ** (attempt - 1));\nconst delay = Math.max(Number.isFinite(retryAfter) ? retryAfter : 0, exp / 2 + Math.random() * (exp / 2));\n\nreturn {\n  json: {\n    attempt,\n    outcome,\n    status_code: status || null,\n    error: outcome === 'success' ? null : (networkError ?? `HTTP ${status}`),\n    retry: outcome === 'transient' && attempt < req.max_attempts,\n    delay_seconds: Math.round(delay * 10) / 10,\n    response: $json.body ?? null,\n  },\n};\n",
        "mode": "runOnceForEachItem"
      },
      "id": "3028385f-85b0-5be5-9c19-29a4a73dbde1",
      "name": "Evaluate attempt",
